# Run output — regenerated by run_benchmark.{ps1,sh} and sweep_repeats_win.sh on every run
# (hundreds of MB of State/DSMCState files). Only the parsed CSVs under results/ are tracked.
results/run_*/
results/sweep_*/
logs/
driver_full.log

# Measured data — re-included against the repo-root `*.csv` rule. This is the
# benchmark's actual result; RESULTS.md / LINUX_RESULTS.md are derived from it.
!results/win_timings.csv
!results/linux_timings.csv

# Frozen benchmark inputs: re-include the .h5 files that the repo-root .gitignore
# excludes. These MUST stay committed — Windows and Linux have to solve a
# byte-identical problem, so the mesh and BGField are shipped, never regenerated.
!pic_hempt_hdg/HEMPT_90deg_BGField.h5
!pic_hempt_hdg/pre-hopr/90_deg_segment_mesh.h5
!dsmc_periodic3d/pre-hopr/periodic_mesh.h5

# Re-run CSVs (2026-07-29 repeatability session) are tracked alongside the baseline.
!results/win_timings_rerun_o1.csv
!results/win_timings_rerun_o3.csv

# Fixed-configuration sweep (2026-07-30): petsc-msmpi-O3 + OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1, 3 repeats
# per point. `_fixed.csv` holds the medians, `_fixed_raw.csv` every repetition — keep both, the
# spread is the evidence that these points are trustworthy where single runs were not.
!results/win_timings_fixed.csv
!results/win_timings_fixed_raw.csv

# PETSc -log_view dumps, 2026-07-30. These are the per-kernel Count/Flop/Mflop/s tables.
# Count and Flop are algorithmic and match across OSes, so the Mflop/s column is a
# drift-free per-kernel speed comparison — this is what identified VecAXPY (OpenBLAS) as
# the PIC gap. `git check-ignore -v` verified on the Windows side: all six are trackable.
# Do not delete these; the whole conclusion rests on them.
!results/logview_linux_bjacobi_1rank.txt
!results/logview_linux_bjacobi_1rank_petscO1.txt
!results/logview_win_bjacobi_1rank.txt
!results/logview_win_bjacobi_1rank_petscO3.txt
!results/logview_win_bjacobi_1rank_blas1thread.txt
!results/logview_win_bjacobi_4rank.txt

# Compiled Linux helper from the THP test: build with `gcc -O2 -o thpon thpon.c` on Linux.
# The source is tracked, the ELF binary is not.
thpon

# CPU-vs-GPU A/B (gpu_ab_win.sh, ABBA-ordered). Raw only — medians live in RESULTS.md.
!results/win_timings_gpu_raw.csv
